Z||000000||HummelHund||07-20-2001||02:24 PM||||I've got to get replacement power window and power mirror switches for my '84 SE. I've found a great junkyard (read: cheap with 7 fieros) in my area, but only one of the Fieros there had power windows and the switches were shot. My question is, did any other GM car use these switches? I've looked and haven't found any yet. Thanks for any help y'all can give me.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE 2M4 WS6 (restoration project to become daily driver)<BR>'84 Sport Coupe ($150 running car)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick86GT||07-20-2001||06:01 PM||||My buddy replaced his w/ later model Grand Am switches bought at a junkyard. While ever so slightly smaller, they look really good. He also install the express down circuit, which is a very convenient feature.<P>I know he has a posting somewhere on this forum that shows pix and describes what he did. email him @ billo@aol.com||||reg||1
